    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1658">

                <pb facs="1057" n="941" xml:id="pg941"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 817.00/2327.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister Jefferson.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 35.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-07-14">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 14, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Upon request of the Minister of Nicaragua
                    at Washington, who had received a telegram from his Government to the effect
                    that Clifford D. Sands had led an unsuccessful attack on the barracks at
                    Bluefields, the Consul at that place was instructed by a telegram dated July 7
                    to report regarding the matter, and replied in a telegram dated July 9 that
                    Sands was brought into the Consulate at 1 o’clock a.m., July 6, badly wounded,
                    and was delivered to the authorities and sent to a hospital on July 8.</p>
                <p>A copy of a memorandum<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1658-f1"/> from the Minister of
                    Nicaragua at Washington, in relation to the matter, is enclosed herewith for
                    your information.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/> [Not signed.]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
